# TradeAgent, unattended: the app on its own display, under an account of its own, started again after a
# crash or a stop. A template: packaging/linux/install.sh fills its placeholders in and installs it root-owned
# in /etc/systemd/system, beside the app's root-owned files under /opt/tradeagent — so the app's own
# account, which is also the agent's, cannot change what systemd starts or what it runs.
#
#   - The stop is the app's own quit: SIGTERM to the app alone (KillMode=mixed), which holds it until the
#     AI has stopped and the ledgers are closed, bounded at 15 s by the app (AppHost.QuitBound); whatever
#     is left of the unit after that, an AI turn's tree included, is killed with the unit's cgroup.
#   - The day is the owner's: TZ is his zone, not the server's UTC — the daily report and the AI's daily
#     spending cap turn at his midnight.
#   - TMPDIR is inside the account's 0700 home: it is where .NET puts the gateway's pipe socket, and no
#     other account can reach into it.
#   - Delegate=yes gives the unit's cgroup to the account (U-cell-linux-b): the app moves itself into
#     supervisor/ and starts each AI launch in an attempt-<id>/ cgroup of its own, so every process of a
#     launch is born there whatever session it makes, and cgroup.kill ends all of it. This line is the only
#     root-owned part; the app never uses sudo. Without it a cell is refused, naming this line.
#   - A CRASH LOOP STOPS (U-service-limits; R31 D12 § H). Restart=always brings the app back 10 s after it dies — short, so
#     a single crash costs ten seconds of the tape and CI's kill -9 check (recording again within 30 s) holds. Before this
#     unit had no start limit, and systemd's default (5 starts in 10 s) never trips at 10 s spacing, so a crash at start-up
#     restarted it every 10-20 s for ever, each start running the cell benchmark and resuming the AI. Now: at most 6 starts
#     in any 10-minute window (systemd's window is fixed: it opens at the first start after the last one ended). A loop whose
#     runs last under about 90 s (six runs and their 10 s restarts inside 600 s) reaches the 7th start inside it, and systemd
#     leaves the unit failed within 10 minutes of the loop's first start, its journal saying "Start request repeated too
#     quickly" (its Result stays the last run's, e.g. 'signal', on systemd 255); nothing restarts it.
#     Every start counts, a hand one too (systemd's documentation); `systemctl reset-failed tradeagent.service` empties the
#     count, and a hand start is accepted again once the window has run out. The kit and tools/linux-host.sh run reset-failed
#     before their own start, so a hand install always starts. A slower loop is the app's own half: a start soon after one
#     that did not close properly waits before the AI works on its own, ten minutes doubling per start in a row, at most
#     two hours (AppHost, CrashWait).
#     Fixed, not growing (RestartSteps= needs systemd 254): the window bounds the loop either way.
[Unit]
Description=TradeAgent on display :@DISPLAY@
Requires=tradeagent-display.service
After=tradeagent-display.service network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target
StartLimitIntervalSec=600
StartLimitBurst=6

[Service]
Type=simple
User=@ACCOUNT@
Group=@ACCOUNT@
UMask=0077
WorkingDirectory=@HOME@
Environment=HOME=@HOME@
Environment=DISPLAY=:@DISPLAY@
Environment=XAUTHORITY=@HOME@/.Xauthority
Environment=TZ=@ZONE@
Environment=TMPDIR=@HOME@/tmp
ExecStart=@ROOT@/current/TradeAgent
Restart=always
RestartSec=10
KillMode=mixed
Delegate=yes
TimeoutStopSec=30

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
